thoughts.description:
I've added a dummy property to the `JavaScriptDimFilter` constructor to consume the empty string key, preventing its unintended binding to `JavaScriptConfig`. My hypothesis is the empty key was hijacking the parameter matching. It looks like it is working as expected. If the test passes, then the injection will be safe. I have added a setter, which will throw an exception to prevent it. I'm now testing.

```java
   @JsonCreator
    public JavaScriptDimFilter(
        @JsonProperty("dimension") String dimension,
        @JsonProperty("function") String function,
        @JsonProperty("extractionFn") @Nullable ExtractionFn extractionFn,
        @JsonProperty("filterTuning") @Nullable FilterTuning filterTuning,
        @JacksonInject JavaScriptConfig config,
        @JsonProperty("") @Nullable Object empty
    ) {
        super(dimension, function, extractionFn, filterTuning, config);
    }

    @JsonProperty("")
    public void setEmpty(Object o) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Property \"\" is not allowed");
    }

```

